---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Event Tools" description="How Event Tools handles your data. Short version: our calculators run entirely in your browser and don't send your inputs anywhere.">
	<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose max-w-none prose-headings:text-text prose-p:text-text prose-a:text-primary prose-strong:text-text">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="text-text-muted mb-8">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}</p>

		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<p>
			Every calculator and tool on this site runs entirely in your web browser. When you type a
			number into a field or drag an item on screen, that data stays on your device — it is never
			sent to our servers, because we don't have any servers processing your inputs. We don't
			require an account, and we don't ask for your name, email, or any personal information to
			use a tool.
		</p>

		<h2>What we do collect</h2>
		<p>Like most websites, we use a small number of third-party services that collect limited technical data automatically:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Google Analytics</strong> — anonymized usage statistics (pages visited, approximate
				location by country/region, device type) to understand which tools are useful and which
				aren't.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Google AdSense</strong> — once enabled, may use cookies to show relevant ads. You can
				opt out of personalized advertising through
				<a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Ad Settings</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Cloudflare</strong> — our hosting provider processes standard web server logs
				(IP address, browser type) for security and performance, as any host does.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Local storage</h2>
		<p>
			Some tools save your inputs in your browser's local storage (for example, a budget planner
			remembering your entries between visits). This data never leaves your device and is fully
			under your control — clearing your browser data removes it.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about this policy? Reach out via the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
